// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`a chat without decisions, constraints or tasks sends what it did before the assembler 1`] = `
{
  "history": [
    {
      "content": "What next?",
      "role": "user",
    },
  ],
  "options": {
    "system": "<artifacts>
When your answer includes a standalone piece the user will likely keep, copy, save or edit (a document, report, plan, letter or article over about 15 lines; a code file or script over about 20 lines; an HTML page; an SVG image; a Mermaid diagram), put it in an artifact instead of the chat text: <artifact id="short-kebab-id" type="markdown|code|html|svg|mermaid|react" title="Short title" language="ts">…the content…</artifact>.
Use language only for type code. Keep explanations outside the tag; the content is shown in a side panel, so don't repeat it in the chat. Snippets, short examples and quick answers stay in the chat as usual.
A react artifact is one component file with a default export. It can import only react (no other packages, no network), so style it with inline styles or a <style> element.
To change an artifact you made earlier in this conversation, send the whole new content with the same id; it becomes a new version.
</artifacts>

The user set these custom instructions. Follow them unless they ask otherwise in the conversation. Narrower instructions take priority: this chat over the project, the project over the general ones.

<about_the_user>
I live in Leeds.
</about_the_user>

<how_to_answer>
Be brief.
</how_to_answer>

<project>
Prices in GBP.
</project>

<this_chat>
Metric units.
</this_chat>

<memories>
Facts about the user that they asked to be remembered across chats. Use them when they help; don't list them back or mention this note. If the conversation contradicts one, the conversation wins.
- Has a dog called Biscuit.
- Likes Shaker-style doors.
</memories>

<earlier_conversation>
A summary of the earlier part of this conversation, which is no longer shown in full. Treat it as what was said before the messages below.
They want a new kitchen.
</earlier_conversation>

<edited_artifacts>
The user changed these artifacts after you last wrote them. This is their current content; build on it (same id) rather than on your earlier version.
<artifact id="plan" type="markdown" title="Plan">
1. Measure
2. Order
</artifact>
</edited_artifacts>",
  },
}
`;
